 "finding": "The elicitation packet filename carried a DATE and no time while the reports it derives from carried a timestamp. Multiple report runs per day each overwrote the packet; the last one survived. This is the seventh instance of the artifact-overwrite class found on 2026-08-04 and the only one known to have destroyed evidence rather than risked it.",
 "why_it_is_not_recoverable": "A row's packet name is derivable from the report it names, by prefix substitution. Zero of the 96 derive to a file that exists. The inputs were not merely unrecorded - the files were overwritten and are gone. RPAS-26 Amendment 2026-08-04b calls these entries unidentified; destroyed is the accurate word.",
